## Local development

Start the site from the repo root:

```bash
npm start
# or: npx serve . -l 3000
```

**Always give the user these local URLs to review before any deploy or push.**

| Page | Local URL |
|------|-----------|
| Home | http://localhost:3000/ |
| Army Builder | http://localhost:3000/projects/army-builder/ |
| HIIT Timer | http://localhost:3000/projects/hiit-timer/ |
| Stratagem Sleeves | http://localhost:3000/projects/stratagem-sleeves/ |
| Tyranids QRS | http://localhost:3000/projects/tyranid-qrs/ |
| Market Day | http://localhost:3000/projects/stock-game/ |

Short paths (`/army-builder/`, etc.) only work on Netlify — use `/projects/<slug>/` locally.

## Deploy gate (mandatory)

**Never push or deploy until the user has reviewed on the local server.**

1. Ensure the daemon is up (`npm run serve:daemon` / `npm run serve:status`) or tell them to run `npm start`
2. Give the relevant **http://localhost:3000/...** link(s)
3. Wait for them to check (or explicitly waive) before `git push` / deploy

Do not skip this even if they say “GO”, “deploy”, or “push” in the same breath — still point them at localhost first unless they clearly say they already checked locally.

## Defaults for agents

- Scope changes to the relevant project folder unless editing the home page or Netlify config
- User-specific saved data goes in browser localStorage, not the repo
- Create commits when completing work; push only when asked (and only after the deploy gate above)
- See `AGENTS.md` for full instructions; see `projects/<slug>/README.md` for project details

